From d1bb2ea9aa9e16d6bf5ec35079fd2ee1e36f85c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Prashant-thakur77 <prashant101007@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 02:12:36 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat: #2426 accept raw calldata on POST
 /api/execute/contract-call

Execution frameworks hand their executor an already-encoded data field.
Accept it in place of functionName and functionArgs: contractCallInputSchema
validates data (0x-prefixed hex, whole bytes, four bytes or more) and requires
a function key only in its absence, then the route decodes it against the body
or explorer ABI into the canonical function key and typed functionArgs and
takes the existing read, simulate and write paths, so the stablecoin cap, the
payable check, the spending caps and the execution record all keep reading a
named function with typed arguments.

The decode is lossless or it is refused. The broadcast is rebuilt from the
decoded arguments rather than the submitted bytes, so the calldata is
re-encoded and compared, and trailing bytes, non-minimal offsets and
non-canonical padding answer 400 rather than being dropped silently.

Nothing is guessed: decoding runs against the caller-supplied ABI alone, with
no signature-database lookup, so a selector the ABI does not contain is a 400
on field data and no guessed signature reaches the signing path.
